      "text": "Using the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials), we can expand the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\).\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) &= 3x^2(7 - 2x) - 5x(7 - 2x) + 4(7 - 2x) \\\\\n&= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x \\\\\n&= -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28 \\\\\n&= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThus, comparing \\(-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\\) to \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), we have:\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28.\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n8a &= 8(-6) = -48, \\\\\n4b &= 4(31) = 124, \\\\\n2c &= 2(-43) = -86, \\\\\nd &= 28.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28.\n\\]\n\nFirst, combine the positive terms:\n\\[\n124 - 86 = 38.\n\\]\n\nNext, combine the results with the negative terms:\n\\[\n-48 + 38 + 28 = 28.\n\\]\n\nThus, \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d = \\boxed{28}\\).",
