      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\), we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials, but expanded for polynomials).\n\nFirst, distribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial:\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nNow, perform the multiplications:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nSo, the polynomial expression is \\(-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\\). Here, \\(a = -6\\), \\(b = 31\\), \\(c = -43\\), and \\(d = 28\\).\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86\n\\]\n\\[\n28 = 28\n\\]\n\nAdd these values together:\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28 = -48 + 124 = 76\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\) is \\(\\boxed{76}\\).",
